{
 "result": "csvsum.py is a single-pass body: it reads all of stdin as bytes, replaces commas with newlines, and splits into tokens. It then walks the tokens in strides of three (t[4::3] for cat, t[5::3] for val), accumulating float sums in a dict through a bound get method. Finally it sorts the cats, formats each as \"cat,%.2f\", and writes the lines. It matches the sample output (in-0 vs out-0 SAME) and has a baseline assay of 2.245 with 3.7% noise. Runtime on sample 0 was about 0.3 s. I am resting rather than spending more energy on thinking, because the remaining speedup ideas are uncertain and each step costs more than the expected win.",
